WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:10.916
Assist, AI Search, agents, and AI in dashboards all run on Worklynq AI credits. In this video, you’ll see how credits work, and keep an eye on them.

2
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:19.061
In the Admin console, open Credits, under AI Monitoring. At the top is what your company has used this month.

3
00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:27.628
Each person gets their own monthly credits with your plan: three thousand on Advance. A typical Assist question uses about nine.

4
00:00:28.067 --> 00:00:39.651
People are warned at eighty percent. When their own credits run out, they carry on with the company’s extra credits, then stop. Only the AI pauses. The rest of Worklynq keeps working.

5
00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:47.673
Extra credits are shared by everyone, and are for this month only. You can see who bought each pack, and click Buy credits for more.

6
00:00:48.133 --> 00:00:55.899
By person shows everyone’s credits against their own. Here, Sam has gone over, and used six hundred and forty extra credits.

7
00:00:56.333 --> 00:01:02.115
By feature shows where the credits go: Assist, AI Search, dashboards, reports and agents.

8
00:01:02.567 --> 00:01:11.548
If your company uses its own Claude or OpenAI key for a feature, that use costs no Worklynq credits. Your provider bills you directly.

9
00:01:12.633 --> 00:01:21.977
Everyone can check their own credits. Open your profile menu and choose AI Usage, to see what’s left, what it was used on, and every recent request.

10
00:01:22.433 --> 00:01:31.265
Credits start again on the first of each month, and unused ones don’t carry over. To change anyone’s monthly credits, contact Worklynq support.

11
00:01:32.633 --> 00:01:42.809
That’s AI credits. Next in the Admin console series: restoring tickets and docs from the trash. You’ll find every guide at worklynq.com/docs.

